  "readOnlyHint": false,
  "title": "imagepeek: make thumbnails of an image"
 },
 "description": "imagepeek: Make 1-8 thumbnails of an image in one call. For one exact resize use image_resize. Returns 1-8 thumbnails in one call, each `sizes` entry {width, height} (at most 4096), by `fit` cover (smart centre crop with `gravity`, default) or contain; not upscaled unless `upscale`. The 15 MB output cap covers all of them together. The images come back in `images`. Reads PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, TIFF, BMP, ICO and AVIF; other formats and images over 40 megapixels are refused (not charged). Output: base64 `data_base64`, without EXIF, GPS, XMP or IPTC; over 15 MB or 50 megapixels is a 413 (not charged). Images are not logged; a result is kept only with `output` \"url\" (24 h). Typically 0.5-2 s. Price: USD 0.002. Free: 3 imagepeek calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/image-thumbnail-api.html",
 "inputSchema": {
